				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## 2026-10-22 prototype/target-model decision — implementation blocked before source edits\nThis user decision supersedes the older in-place consolidation plan above: retain the existing class identity as CRConfigurationPrototype, create a NEW CRConfiguration directly under CFConfiguration with no local parent slot, then deliberately migrate reviewed Runtime subclasses/callers. Do not copy Foundation-owned behavior into the new Runtime base, fix upstream tools, introduce temporary slots, or use evaluation to mutate class identities. Prototype evidence is not a second supported implementation; remaining experimental consumers need an explicit review/removal condition.\n\nExact blocker in this Maintainer child's exposed tool set: there is no class-rename tool. changeClassOrTraitSignature selects an EXISTING targetClassName; GtLClassChangeDataExtractor>>extractTargetClassIfError: resolves that name from globals and supplies no old-name/new-name pair. createClassesAndTraits cannot replace the occupied CRConfiguration name: GtLClassCreationDataExtractor>>extractTargetClassNameIfError: rejects existing globals. Therefore the required first operation cannot safely be expressed. No rename, create, signature change, method compilation/removal, class removal, workaround or automatic rollback was attempted. Source manifest is empty across CatalystFoundation and CatalystRuntime. New target hierarchy and required protocol corrections remain unmet; passing baseline checks do not change that outcome.\n\nInitial checkpoint succeeded: current child continuity ID cff5ab9a-f391-4013-bfe3-b951724649d7, continuity not degraded. Exact active Maintainer is this child, execution 86qaee8aqhxx1dt8mnsha3qon under owner c2211feb-aa08-419a-acbf-fba0b93a4ffb; identity reconciled by finding this run's retained evidence in its own object storage and matching its request. Other retained Maintainers observed idle with no pending Barry UI. No process/gate reset, cancellation or delegation. Inspectable owner for this run's objects: c2211feb-aa08-419a-acbf-fba0b93a4ffb/86qaee8aqhxx1dt8mnsha3qon. Combined source/blocker evidence {{gtObject:id=4awdspvel24j8yzynmsdeuzpu|fallbackLabelString='Prototype sprint blocked source and ownership evidence'}}; ownership {{gtObject:id=cju9j6na68g7e8tmui1lk1iif|fallbackLabelString='Current child checkpoint and exact identity'}}; dispatch scan {{gtObject:id=7gx7orufy573ipi1u6uxf27ye|fallbackLabelString='Required configuration dispatch source scan'}}.\n\nObserved hierarchy remains CRConfiguration under CFLabelledObject, local parent, 15 direct subclasses (including CRFailureEvidenceOverride); CRConfigurationPrototype absent. Zero consumers migrated, zero instances deliberately migrated. Class-reference and literal-search tools returned no CRConfiguration method matches; this does NOT establish no consumers: subclass discovery and dynamic codec construction must also be reviewed. Full instance census, codec-name compatibility and complete string-source consumer review were not completed before the blocker. Do not claim automatic preservation/migration of existing parent values.\n\nBehavior allocation from inspected base source: Foundation already owns parent/parent:/hasParent/initialize/rootConfiguration/ancestorConfigurations and must supply these by inheritance, not copying. Generic nearest-first predicate ancestry search belongs with Foundation ancestry; withParent: is generic construction. Runtime defaultWithParent: must retain self default dispatch (Foundation currently self new); assess default construction collaboration before moving it. Runtime-specific asEffectiveConfiguration, configurationSnapshotUsing:, validateSemanticsOn: remain Runtime responsibilities, distinct from Foundation graph validation and planner projection. Prototype ancestry starts via self parent whereas Foundation currently starts at the slot: preserving accessor overrides requires a Foundation correction and focused check, not a duplicate Runtime method. firstAncestorConfigurationOfClass: currently uses a class predicate and has an identified UI caller CRHostServiceIdentifierAddStencil>>runtimeConfiguration; replacing it requires a domain collaboration, not renaming the predicate. No behavior moved in this blocked run.\n\nRequired production class dispatch is still present: CFConfigurationAsset>>validateMaterializedConfiguration:, CFConfigurationCodec class>>representationFor:/encodeValue:/fromRepresentation:/decodeObject:, CFConfigurationGraphCopier>>copyValue:forDescription:/copyEditingValuesFrom:, CFConfigurationPlanner>>placementsForConfigurationsIn:asset:visited:into:/placementsFor:inMemento:visited:into:, CFConfigurationValidator>>validateMagritteConfigurationsIn:visited:on:. Declared asset/MA relation type validation and unsupported-value rejection are semantic constraints, not permission to silently remove validation. CRConfigurationSnapshot already delegates value-specific native copying through configurationSnapshotUsing: after its bounded built-in handling and rejects unsupported values; it must not become the planner copier. No replacement protocol chosen or implemented without completing caller/collaborator review."
			},
